{"slug":"auth","title":"Auth & roles","blocks":[
{"id":"b1","type":"ingress","content":[{"type":"text","value":"Barkpark uses bearer-token API tokens ("},{"type":"text","value":"Authorization: Bearer <token>","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":") backed by "},{"type":"text","value":"api_tokens","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" (SHA256 token hash + permission list per token)."}]},
{"id":"b2","type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","value":"Barkpark uses bearer-token API tokens ("},{"type":"text","value":"Authorization: Bearer <token>","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":") backed by "},{"type":"text","value":"api_tokens","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" (SHA256 token hash + permission list per token). Browser LiveViews read the same token from "},{"type":"text","value":"session[\"api_token\"]","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" via the "},{"type":"text","value":"BarkparkWeb.LiveAuth","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" "},{"type":"text","value":"on_mount","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" hooks."}]},
{"id":"b3","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Tenancy — token ↔ workspace"},
{"id":"b4","type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","value":"The principal of a request is the API token; every token is bound to exactly one "},{"type":"text","value":"workspace","marks":["strong"]},{"type":"text","value":" (the tenancy boundary; see the Workspace → Project → Dataset hierarchy in "},{"type":"text","value":"docs/api-v1.md","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" §1a). The binding is two facts that must agree:"}]},
{"id":"b5","type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[
[{"type":"text","value":"api_tokens.workspace_id","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" — the workspace the token belongs to."}],
[{"type":"text","value":"a "},{"type":"text","value":"workspace_memberships","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" row — the token's principal is a member of that workspace."}]
]},
{"id":"b6","type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","value":"Content/data requests carry the workspace + project in the path ("},{"type":"text","value":"/w/:workspace_slug/p/:project_slug/v1/data/...","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":"). The server resolves the workspace and project from the path and enforces tenancy "},{"type":"text","value":"before","marks":["strong"]},{"type":"text","value":" any permission check:"}]},
{"id":"b7","type":"table","head":[[{"type":"text","value":"Situation"}],[{"type":"text","value":"Result"}]],"rows":[
[[{"type":"text","value":":workspace_slug","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" does not resolve to a workspace"}],[{"type":"text","value":"404 not_found","marks":["code"]}]],
[[{"type":"text","value":"Workspace resolves, but the token has no "},{"type":"text","value":"workspace_memberships","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" row for it"}],[{"type":"text","value":"403 forbidden","marks":["code"]}]],
[[{"type":"text","value":"Workspace resolves and the token is a member"}],[{"type":"text","value":"proceed to permission checks below"}]]
]},
{"id":"b8","type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","value":"Every content read and write is scoped by the resolved workspace — a token can only see and mutate documents in its own workspace. There is no cross-workspace read."}]},
{"id":"b9","type":"heading","level":3,"text":"Write gate"},
{"id":"b10","type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","value":"The core mutate endpoint ("},{"type":"text","value":"POST /w/:workspace_slug/p/:project_slug/v1/data/mutate/:dataset","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":") enforces the "},{"type":"text","value":"write","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" permission "},{"type":"text","value":"after","marks":["strong"]},{"type":"text","value":" tenancy passes. A token that is a valid member lacking "},{"type":"text","value":"write","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" (a read-only token) gets "},{"type":"text","value":"403 forbidden","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" on mutate; reads remain available."}]},
{"id":"b11","type":"heading","level":3,"text":"Default workspace + flat alias"},
{"id":"b12","type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","value":"Flat content paths ("},{"type":"text","value":"/v1/data/:dataset/*","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":", etc.) still work, resolving to the "},{"type":"text","value":"\"Default\"","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" workspace/project (existing content auto-backfilled). The dev token below is a "},{"type":"text","value":"Default","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" member, so flat-route callers work unchanged."}]},
{"id":"b13","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Roles (permissions list on ApiToken.permissions)"},
{"id":"b14","type":"table","head":[[{"type":"text","value":"Permission"}],[{"type":"text","value":"Grants"}],[{"type":"text","value":"Surfaces"}]],"rows":[
[[{"type":"text","value":"read","marks":["code"]}],[{"type":"text","value":"Public reads on private datasets / private schemas"}],[{"type":"text","value":"/w/:workspace_slug/p/:project_slug/v1/data/query/*","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" (flat alias "},{"type":"text","value":"/v1/data/query/*","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":"), "},{"type":"text","value":"/media","marks":["code"]}]],
[[{"type":"text","value":"write","marks":["code"]}],[{"type":"text","value":"Mutations (create, patch, publish, unpublish, delete)"}],[{"type":"text","value":"POST /w/:workspace_slug/p/:project_slug/v1/data/mutate/:dataset","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" (flat alias "},{"type":"text","value":"POST /v1/data/mutate/:dataset","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":"), "},{"type":"text","value":"POST /media/upload","marks":["code"]}]],
[[{"type":"text","value":"ops","marks":["code"]}],[{"type":"text","value":"Operate the Bokbasen publish pipeline (read-only on plugin secrets)"}],[{"type":"text","value":"/admin/onixedit/bokbasen","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" LiveView (old "},{"type":"text","value":"/admin/bokbasen","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" 301-redirects here)"}]],
[[{"type":"text","value":"admin","marks":["code"]}],[{"type":"text","value":"All of the above + plugin-settings reveal/audit + schema CRUD"}],[{"type":"text","value":"/studio/settings","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"text","value":"/v1/schemas/*","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"text","value":"/v1/plugins/settings/*","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"text","value":"/v1/webhooks/*","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"text","value":"/v1/plugins/onixedit/export/*","marks":["code"]}]]
]},
{"id":"b15","type":"heading","level":3,"text":"Hierarchy"},
{"id":"b16","type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","value":"admin","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" is a "},{"type":"text","value":"superset","marks":["strong"]},{"type":"text","value":" of every other permission. Granting "},{"type":"text","value":"admin","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" grants "},{"type":"text","value":"ops","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" (and "},{"type":"text","value":"read","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" + "},{"type":"text","value":"write","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" for routes that check those plugs). The "},{"type":"text","value":"BarkparkWeb.LiveAuth.:ops","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" hook accepts either "},{"type":"text","value":"ops","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" or "},{"type":"text","value":"admin","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":", which means existing admin tokens keep working unchanged when an "},{"type":"text","value":"ops","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":"-gated route is added (Phase 8 WI5 backwards-compat)."}]},
{"id":"b17","type":"heading","level":3,"text":"Why :ops is separate from :admin"},
{"id":"b18","type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","value":"The Bokbasen publish console ("},{"type":"text","value":"/admin/onixedit/bokbasen","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":", an OnixEdit plugin-contributed LiveView; old "},{"type":"text","value":"/admin/bokbasen","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" 301-redirects here) needs to be operated by people who should "},{"type":"text","value":"not","marks":["strong"]},{"type":"text","value":" be able to read the encrypted Bokbasen "},{"type":"text","value":"client_secret","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" (which is what "},{"type":"text","value":"/studio/settings","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" exposes via the plugin-secret reveal flow). Splitting "},{"type":"text","value":"ops","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" out lets a publishing operator see submission status, retry failed jobs, and inspect last errors — without ever holding the "},{"type":"text","value":"admin","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" permission."}]},
{"id":"b19","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"LiveView on_mount hooks"},
{"id":"b20","type":"code","value":"# api/lib/barkpark_web/live_auth.ex\non_mount :admin   # → requires \"admin\"\non_mount :ops     # → requires \"ops\" OR \"admin\""},
{"id":"b21","type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","value":"Both halt with a flash + redirect to "},{"type":"text","value":"/studio","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" when the session token is missing, malformed, or lacks the required permission."}]},
{"id":"b22","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Plug pipelines (HTTP)"},
{"id":"b23","type":"code","value":"# api/lib/barkpark_web/router.ex\npipeline :require_token  # → BarkparkWeb.Plugs.RequireToken\npipeline :require_admin  # → RequireToken + RequireAdmin"},
{"id":"b24","type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","value":"There is no "},{"type":"text","value":"require_ops","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" plug today — the only ops surface is a LiveView, so the "},{"type":"text","value":"on_mount","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" gate is sufficient. Add a plug here if HTTP-only operator endpoints land."}]},
{"id":"b25","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Dev token"},
{"id":"b26","type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","value":"barkpark-dev-token","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" (seeded in "},{"type":"text","value":"priv/repo/seeds.exs","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":") carries "},{"type":"text","value":"[\"read\", \"write\", \"admin\"]","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" and is bound to the "},{"type":"text","value":"Default","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" workspace (with a "},{"type":"text","value":"workspace_memberships","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" row), so it satisfies every gate in this document and works on both the scoped and flat-alias routes. Production deployments should issue narrower tokens per persona (publisher gets "},{"type":"text","value":"ops","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":"; everyone else gets "},{"type":"text","value":"read","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":"/"},{"type":"text","value":"write","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" without "},{"type":"text","value":"admin","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" or "},{"type":"text","value":"ops","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":"), each bound to the workspace its principal belongs to."}]},
{"id":"b27","type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","value":"MUST rotate before prod","marks":["strong"]},{"type":"text","value":" (rescued from the "},{"type":"text","value":"create-barkpark-app","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" starter templates): the dev token has read + write + admin scopes and "},{"type":"text","value":"must not be used in production","marks":["strong"]},{"type":"text","value":" — rotate it before deploying. The starter templates bake "},{"type":"text","value":"barkpark-dev-token","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" into both "},{"type":"text","value":"BARKPARK_TOKEN","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"text","value":"BARKPARK_SERVER_TOKEN","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" env examples; a production deploy must replace "},{"type":"text","value":"both","marks":["strong"]},{"type":"text","value":" with freshly-issued tokens."}]}
],"related":["api-v1"]}
